gTI(){return"Contact"},
gTJ(){return"What the wristband measures: heart rate, heart rate variability (HRV), blood oxygen (SpO2), ECG, sleep, steps, workouts, body temperature, stress and estimated blood pressure. What you enter: age, height, weight, sex, body composition and reminders. The wristband's Bluetooth address. We don't ask for your name, national ID number, phone or email; on the portal you are known only by a random pseudonym. If you fill in the partnership form on our website, your name, organisation, email and message are stored encrypted only so we can reply; they are never combined with health data. The pre-registration form takes only your email, used for a single announcement when the app reaches the stores."},
gTK(){return"What data do we process?"},
gTL(){return"Draft: this text has not been reviewed by a lawyer. The data controller's name, address and retention periods will be added before release."},
gTM(){return"This text explains how the Bileklik app and portal process your personal data under the Turkish Personal Data Protection Law No. 6698 (KVKK)."},
gTN(){return"Health data is a special category of personal data and is processed with your explicit consent (KVKK Article 6). Each sharing needs its own consent: you choose who sees which types and for how long, and you can withdraw consent at any time."},
gTO(){return"Legal basis"},
gTP(){return"To show you your measurements; to share them with the doctors, research institutions and family members you choose; and, if you want, to write them to Apple Health or Health Connect. Your data is not used for advertising and is not sold."},
gTQ(){return"Why do we process it?"},
gTR(){return"Data on your phone stays until you delete the app. Measurements on the portal stay until you delete them; when a consent ends, that follower can no longer see them. Access logs are kept after deletion because of legal retention duties."},
gTS(){return"How long is it kept?"},
gTT(){return"Under KVKK Article 11 you can ask whether your data is processed, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and withdraw consent. In the app you can remove sharing under Profile > Doctors and research and Profile > Health community, delete your portal data under Profile > Portal account, and get all your data as a FHIR file under Profile > Export my data."},
gTU(){return"Your rights"},
gTV(){return"Only the doctors, research institutions or family group members you consent to, only the types you choose and only for the consent period. Values you enter yourself, such as weight and body composition, are shared only if you separately choose \u201cBody measurements\u201d. Only the types you choose are written to Apple Health or Health Connect; the app does not read data from them. Feedback is not linked to your identity. When something stands out in the types you share (for example SpO2 stays low or no data has arrived for a day), the portal shows your doctor an automatic alert; these alerts are not a diagnosis and are deleted when you delete your portal data. If you also turn on \u201cAlert the group in an emergency\u201d for a family group, the same alerts for the types you share with that group are shown to its members."},
gTW(){return"Who is it shared with?"},
gTX(){return"Measurements are kept on your phone in an encrypted database whose key lives in the phone's secure area (iOS Keychain, Android Keystore). This data is not included in phone backups. Only the types you choose to share go to the portal, where they are also stored encrypted."},
